      "body": "**CRITICAL: Always use the CLI for object modifications.** Direct edits to instance YAML under `docs/process/` bypass integrity, content-addressed filenames, and caches.\n\n## Requirement\n1. Create, update, and delete instance/process data only via `zqk object create|update|delete` (or the appropriate domain command).\n2. Do not hand-edit YAML under `docs/process/` for instance data. Exception: `docs/process/_internal/` schema/config when CLI or tooling is unavailable — document why and follow up.\n3. After a CLI write, **commit the CAS rename with the work** (`POL-CODE-CAS-COMMIT-001`). Do not leave `complete` / `in_progress` hash YAML untracked.\n\n## Mechanical\nCapability gates (not Cursor `.mdc` prose) enforce CAS integrity:\n- `scripts/check-process-cas-commit-with-work.sh` — unstaged same-id rename pairs fail the commit (`POL-CODE-CAS-COMMIT-001`).\n- `scripts/check-cas-process-staged.sh` — staged hash filename must match blob sha256.\n- `scripts/check-process-casable-staged.sh` — staged instances must have left the draft plane.\n\nVendor IDE rules (`.cursor/rules/process-data-cli-only.mdc` and siblings) are **projections**. If they disagree with this object or `POL-CODE-CAS-COMMIT-001`, trust the kernel.\n",
      "category": "workflow",
      "created_at": "2025-01-02T00:00:00Z",
      "created_by": "ACC-1785920548450214012-68b850c0",
      "effective_date": "2025-01-02",
