    {
      "context": "Peer agents orchestrating subagents on an assigned priority_plan. Lower altitude\nthan TPM (roadmap/multi-plan Gantt). Workstreams encode technical sequencing\n(e.g. dedicated tech-debt lane vs project lane).\n",
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T05:39:08Z",
      "created_by": "ACC-1785920548450214006-2e52b3e7",
      "id": "ASK-1786081148616665000-c78bdd4d",
      "instructions": "Filesystem twin (keep in sync): `.zqk/skills/zqk-orchestration/SKILL.md` (and `skills/zqk-orchestration/`).\nTPM altitude: `.zqk/skills/zqk-expert/references/tpm-orchestration.md`.\n\n# ZQK Orchestration (plan primary)\n\nOperating altitude: **assigned `priority_plan` + its `workstream`s**.  \nTPM altitude (roadmaps, multi-plan Gantt, PR-to-main): `.zqk/skills/zqk-expert/references/tpm-orchestration.md` — do **not** re-plan the portfolio from this seat.\n\nWhen this file disagrees with live CLI / `POL-*`, trust the kernel.\n\n## Your job\n\n1. Own **one** locked (or locking) plan handed by the TPM.\n2. Sequence BLIs/ATKs across the plan’s **workstream lanes** so the swarm stays smooth — no mayhem, no clobbering.\n3. Orchestrate subagents to **plan completion** (`zqk agent orchestrate`, feed steers with hourglass).\n4. Land all code on the **TPM-provisioned plan collaboration branch**; do not invent a second integration trunk or open the PR to `main` unless TPM delegated that explicitly.\n\n## Workstreams as sequencing levers\n\nWorkstreams are long-lived **lanes**, not mini-sprints. Use them to make technical tradeoffs explicit:\n\n| Lane pattern | Why |\n|--------------|-----|\n| Project / feature WS | Delivers the plan’s functional bundle |\n| Tech-debt / hardening WS | Pays down friction so the next feature wave does not stall |\n| Docs / design WS | Specs and research that unblock builders |\n\n**Ask before every wave:** “When did we last spend effort on debt / hardening in the lanes this plan touches?” If the answer is “ages,” sequence a debt BLI (or ATK tranche) **inside the sealed plan** if one exists; if not, escalate to TPM for a **new** plan/column — do **not** stuff draft-plane scope onto an execution-facing plan.\n\nChoose whatever lane split keeps sequencing **intuitive** (backend+infra together, frontend alone, debt dedicated, etc.). Conflict mitigation = separate colliding flavors onto different workstreams or different plans.\n\n## Scope discipline\n\n- Execute the **frozen** BLI set. Mid-flight gaps → escalate (new plan / strategic replan), not silent scope creep.\n- Prefer shovel-ready ATKs derived from plan BLIs; avoid conveyor micro-minting that bypasses the plan.\n- VDS / criteria gates before claiming BLI or plan-slice done.\n\n## Branch + subagent geometry\n\nPolicy: **`POL-CODE-1784784370706305000-e3e7245a`**.\n\n```text\nmain\n  └── integration/pri-\u003cplan\u003e     ← TPM provisioned; your merge target\n        ├── worktree/agent-a     ← subagent\n        └── worktree/agent-b\n```\n\n- Subagents branch/worktree **off the plan branch**, not off `main`.\n- Merge up only after pedantic/build/policy gates.\n- TPM opens the single PR to `main` (auto-merge vs human oversight).\n\n## Mesh / hourglass (mandatory)\n\n- Wake peers: notify/MCP only (`POL-AGENT-MESH-WAKE-001`) — not AppleScript paste.\n- Directed steers: **`--await-peer-ack`** (`POL-AGENT-ORCH-HOURGLASS-001`).\n- Workers: `zqk agent next \u003cATK\u003e --on-validation-failure wake`.\n- Never fire-and-forget a handoff, then idle.\n\n```bash\n./bin/zqk workflow whats-next --format json --agent-id \u003cseat\u003e\n./bin/zqk agent orchestrate          # or plan-scoped variant per CLI help\n./bin/zqk feed steer --to-agent-id \u003cpeer\u003e --await-peer-ack --message \"…\"\n./bin/zqk feed ack --in-reply-to AFE-… --agent-id \u003cseat\u003e\n```\n\n## Escalate to TPM when\n\n- Plan scope is wrong / incomplete for the desired outcome\n- Workstream collision with another active plan\n- No collaboration branch provisioned\n- Debt vs feature balance needs a **new** plan column\n- Ready for PR-to-main / auto-merge criteria judgment\n\n## Anti-patterns\n\n- Acting as TPM: rewriting roadmaps or juggling unrelated PRIs\n- Racing `main` or peers’ branch tips\n- Expanding an `active`/`in_progress` plan with exploring BLIs\n- Ignoring debt lanes until the swarm is stuck in mayhem\n- Vendor subagent tools instead of ZQK orchestrate / feed\n\n## Related\n\n- TPM contract: `.zqk/skills/zqk-expert/references/tpm-orchestration.md`\n- Operating DNA: `.zqk/skills/zqk-expert/SKILL.md`\n- Mesh: `scripts/mesh/README.md`, `WFL-TPM-AGY-MESH-001`\n",
      "instructions_summary": "Plan-primary altitude: assigned PRI + workstream lanes (feature vs tech-debt), subagent swarm to plan completion, plan-branch merges; below TPM Gantt altitude.",
